abstract: >-
  Coastal mangrove forests provide flood protection, yet their economic value
  remains uncertain because traditional engineering-based damage avoidance
  methods may not reflect how private markets actually value these benefits
  during rare disaster events. We develop a valuation framework comparing
  engineering estimates with market-based assessments derived from
  consumption-based asset pricing theory. Using catastrophe risk modeling
  across seven coastal Florida counties, we simulate impacts under four storm
  return periods with and without mangroves. Our market-based approach applies
  a stochastic discount factor calibrated to disaster consumption shocks,
  reflecting households' elevated marginal utility during floods.
keywords:
  - mangroves
  - coastal protection
  - asset pricing
  - flood damages
  - ecosystem services
date-released: 2026-04-27
